# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type | title }})

Provides information about the options of a Bastion configuration file (e.g. `wabengine` for the
global configuration, `bastionadm` for the GUI, `rdpproxy` for the RDP proxy).

## Example Usage

```terraform
data "wallix-bastion_configoption" "global" {
  config_id = "wabengine"
  options_list = [
    "fqdn",
    "am.session_timeout",
  ]
}

output "session_timeout" {
  value     = jsondecode(data.wallix-bastion_configoption.global.values).am.session_timeout
  sensitive = true
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Usage Notes

`config_id` is the id or the name (`config_name`) of the configuration file.

`options_list` restricts the returned options to the listed sections or options
(`<option>`, `<section>`, or `<section>.<option>`); with a section, all its options are returned.
Without it, every option of the configuration file is returned, including images.

The options are returned in two formats:

- `values`: a JSON object of the option values, with an option of a section in a nested object
  named after the section. It is the format of the `values` argument of the
  [`wallix-bastion_configoption`](../resources/configoption.md) resource.
- `options`: the raw API representation, one JSON string per option or section (with the
  `name` and `value` of an option, or the `name` and `options` of a section).
